# Openhand agent continuity

## Context handoff (mandatory)

When the conversation is long / near context limits, or before ending a large multi-topic turn:

1. Update `.cursor/lanes/SYNC.md` if other lanes need the new names, verbs, or inboxes.
2. Optionally append a short diary note to `.cursor/handoff.md` (what changed, open TODOs). Do not treat handoff as the living board.
3. Start or resume other lane threads by reading `.cursor/lanes/SYNC.md` first. Handoff is history only.

## Product priorities

- **Active line: Combat Lab / 踢馆** — climb-first gauntlet. Full picture: `docs/combat/AGENT.md`. Living board: `.cursor/lanes/SYNC.md`.
- Mainline map and exploration are **frozen** (`docs/frozen/`). Do not read or polish unless the user asks.

## Map rules (frozen — only when user explicitly works on map)

- Portals: Chebyshev distance **≥ 3** between any two portals in a scene (enforced in `world.test.ts`).
- Water: no shore overlays; no thin inland streams — connect to rim water or ≥3 wide + long; roads over water use bridges.
- Building names on portal doors; travel doors use horizontal door art.

## When user asks for「大总结 / 大评估」

Unless they explicitly say「地图」, they mean **playability content**:
puzzles, side quests, companions, weapons, enemies, cards, buffs/debuffs, combos, hooks, silver — with counts and a short pros/cons playability verdict.
